get.description:
`status`: pending (waiting for a second approval), applied, rejected, all (the default); `store_id`; newest
first, cursor pages (`per_page` 1–100, default 30). `kinds` — what an adjustment can change, with labels;
`threshold` — from this amount a second member approves.

`status`: open (the default: pending and awaiting_second), pending (no approval yet), awaiting_second (approved
once, waits for another member), completed, rejected, all; `store_id`. Oldest open first, else newest first;
cursor pages (`per_page` 1–100, default 30). `counts` — open requests and their amount.

`q`: up to 20 stores whose name matches; `store_id` + `q`: up to 20 of that store's products by name;
`ids[]` / `product_ids[]`: those stores / products (to show a chosen value's name). Without anything: the first
20 stores by name.

post.description:
`reason` (where the money came from). Only an unpaid (issued) invoice; marking one paid again changes nothing.
The balance does not change: the payment itself is booked as a top-up, which pays the oldest invoices first;
what the ledger has not paid of the invoice stays in the store's subscription debt. Ends the dunning for it.

Owner only (settings.manage). Required as in the panel: `name`, `address`, `region_id`, `district_id` (of that
region), `latitude`, `longitude`. `open_time` and `close_time` ("HH:MM", both or neither): one daily window;
equal times or none = round the clock, closing before opening = overnight (e.g. 18:00–02:00).

get.description:
The tariffs and the branch's calendar (weekend days, ISO 1 = Monday, default Saturday and Sunday; holidays,
Y-m-d). The most specific tariff wins: the room's own, then its kind in its hall, then its kind in the branch;
a holiday without its own price is priced as a weekend, a weekend as a weekday. Without a tariff: no room fee.

The store's default (`branch_id` null) and the branch overrides. A channel list null means `["pos_hall"]`;
Telegram orders never get either fee. P3-12: a row with `hall_id` is that hall's own (it replaces the branch's
in the hall).

post.description:
The line reached the guests: `ready` (the kitchen display bumped it) or `sent` (a station without a display,
e.g. tea) becomes `served`. 422 `already_served`, `item_not_ready` (not sent yet or voided). Needs orders.manage;
the waiter rule applies (`approval_token`).
